Package: hd-docker
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Erik Van Hamme <erik.vanhamme@gmail.com>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: python3, docker.io, docker-cli, docker-buildx, docker-compose, ufw
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Description: HyprDebian Docker support
 Installs Docker, with its command line and buildx, which docker build uses,
 and Docker Compose, and sets them up to work with the ufw firewall.
 .
 /etc/docker/daemon.json gives the bridge of Docker the address
 192.168.253.1/24 and takes the networks of containers from 192.168.240.0/20,
 so they stay clear of the usual home and office networks, and limits the
 open files of containers to 1024, at most 524288, so apt in a container
 stays fast. The rules that
 hd-docker adds to /etc/ufw/after.rules keep the ports that containers
 publish from bypassing ufw: traffic from outside reaches a container only
 when a route rule of ufw allows it, such as ufw route allow.
